Licensing of the material in this repository
============================================

This file DESCRIBES the licence terms the imported material already carries.
It GRANTS NOTHING. CeraLive is not a copyright holder of any patch content here
and is not in a position to license it to anyone.

Read docs/PROVENANCE.md for the full audit, including what we verified, what we
did not, and the open questions. This file is only a summary.


Patch content (upstream/, patches/, overlays/)
----------------------------------------------

Authored by Ross Cawston (https://github.com/rcawston), ported from Rockchip's
BSP MPP driver sources. The upstream repository
https://github.com/rcawston/rockchip-rk3588-mainline-patches has NO licence file
of its own, so licensing information exists only in the per-file headers carried
inside the diffs:

  * New encoder sources        SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
  * New UAPI header            SPDX-License-Identifier:
                                 ((GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note) OR MIT)
  * Device-tree overlay        SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
  * Module metadata            MODULE_LICENSE("Dual MIT/GPL")

  Copyright (C) Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
  Copyright (C) 2026 Ross Cawston

We verified that the Rockchip BSP files these were ported from carry the SAME
SPDX tags, so the dual-licence claim is inherited from the copyright holder
rather than asserted downstream. See docs/PROVENANCE.md section 4.

Files the series MODIFIES rather than adds keep their existing mainline Linux
licence (GPL-2.0 / GPL-2.0-only). The series alters no SPDX line.

CeraLive uses and redistributes this material under the GPL-2.0 branch of the
disjunction above, as ordinary Linux kernel patches. We make NO MIT claim and
take no MIT-dependent action. Relying on the MIT branch would require a
line-by-line derivation audit that has not been performed, plus actual legal
review. See docs/PROVENANCE.md section 5.1.


CeraLive-authored material
--------------------------

Everything under scripts/, docs/, rebase/, .github/, plus kernel-pin.env,
README.md and AGENTS.md, is CeraLive packaging, tooling and documentation. It
contains no patch content. It is offered under GPL-2.0-or-later, matching the
material it exists to package.

  Copyright (C) 2026 CeraLive


No legal review has been performed on any of the above, and none is implied.
